  "question": "Can the original 1951 issue-9 access route be made more redundant by adding an exact NDL second-half original-serial object and an independently cataloged 1986 Wenwu Press facsimile covering the full 1951 volume 2, without pretending either route is already a direct article-text collation?",
  "answer": "Yes. NDL Search directly exposes the paper serial-volume object 《文物参考资料 2(7)-2(12) 1951》 under call number Z8-AC150; because the target issue is volume 2 issue 9, it is explicitly contained in that held range. The reviewed NDL record is a paper-material record and exposes no item-specific digital surrogate target; clicking the generic 'read on the Internet' access-method label led to NDL help rather than target page images, so no digital availability is inferred. Independently, Ryukoku University Library's first-party OPAC records a Wenwu Press facsimile edition, Beijing [1986], 13 volumes, NCID AN10296217, and its Omiya holding 054/638 covers the entire 1951 volume 2. This creates an original-object route plus a later facsimile backup route. Neither Zhao Wanli pp.221–233 nor the six-title wording has been directly read in either object, and the facsimile's page-for-page fidelity to the specific 1951 issue has not been independently collated.",
